OpenAI endpoints: do not reserve requested output tokens in the
prompt-length pre-check.

TokenizeParams computed max_input_tokens = max_total_tokens -
max_output_tokens and rejected any prompt longer than that limit with
a 400 error, so with max_model_len=60000 and max_tokens=10000 every
request whose prompt was longer than 50000 tokens was rejected even
though the prompt itself fits the model's context window. This image
serves a single-user deployment that sends long prompts with a large
max_tokens budget, and it wants the engine to accept every prompt that
fits and simply stop generation at the context boundary
(finish_reason="length").

Add TokenizeParams.reserve_output_tokens (default True, upstream
behavior) and have the chat/completion/responses protocol builders set
it to False: the input pre-check now fires only when the prompt alone
exceeds max_model_len, and the downstream get_max_tokens()
min-clamping already limits actual generation to
max_model_len - input_length. Error messages in reserve mode no longer
claim output tokens were requested against the total.

